  "narrative": "No assessments are due. I continue focused follow-up on the one accepted dataset-specific association, H142: feature_060=1 versus feature_060=0 is associated with stronger outcome_006 dependency when feature_024 is at or above its median. The most important unresolved questions are whether this high-feature_024 signal is genuinely concentrated with feature_034=1, whether feature_034 modifies the feature_060 contrast independently of feature_024, and whether the association remains specific to outcome_006.\n\nDirection convention for all new outcome_006 proposals: hypothesis direction is -1, so a positive returned estimate means feature_060=1 has a more negative raw dependency score than feature_060=0, i.e. stronger dependency. For outcome_006, the 10% threshold is about 0.0175 score units. I use anticipated raw direction 0 for most controls because the scientific question is whether these complementary regions remain null or reveal that the accepted contrast is not confined to the high-feature_024 half.\n\nFirst, I register low-feature_024 feature_034 tests. The low-feature_024 direct interaction by feature_034 is the natural complement to H159. If feature_034 is a main modifier of the feature_060 association, it should show a favorable interaction in the low-feature_024 population as well as, or instead of, the high-feature_024 population. If it is null in low feature_024 but positive in high feature_024, that supports a joint feature_024 x feature_034 concentration rather than a simple feature_034-only interaction. I also register the low-feature_024 simple effect among feature_034=1 to interpret any heterogeneity hidden by the overall low-feature_024 null in H143.\n\nSecond, I add a high-third-quartile feature_034=0 simple effect. This complements H160 and helps interpret the high-third-quartile feature_034 interaction H161. If high-third-quartile feature_034=1 is positive while high-third-quartile feature_034=0 is near null, the signal is better described as feature_060 activity concentrated in the intersection of high feature_024 and feature_034=1, not merely a feature_024 or feature_034 threshold effect.\n\nThird, I test the baseline association of feature_034 with outcome_006 separately in high and low feature_024. Overall feature_034 was only near threshold and imprecise in H19. If feature_034=1 has a clinically meaningful baseline dependency contrast only in high feature_024, the H152 nested feature_060 simple effect may partly reflect overlapping subgroup dependence rather than a distinct feature_060-specific interaction. If feature_034 is null in both halves, that strengthens the case that the promising H152 signal is about feature_060 modification conditional on feature_034, not merely a feature_034 main effect.\n\nFinally, I register outcome specificity in the intersection of high feature_024 and feature_034=1 for outcome_008 and outcome_013. Earlier outcome specificity checks within high feature_024 overall were null, opposite, or below threshold for outcome_008, outcome_011, and outcome_013. Testing the narrower intersection is useful because if outcome_006 is uniquely sensitive, these should remain below their roughly 0.027 to 0.028 clinical thresholds. If one or more other outcomes become clinically favorable only in this intersection, the association is broader but still noncausal and dataset-specific.\n\nI do not reopen closed gradient tails or the broad nominal marker families. The validation budget is reserved for the feature_024/feature_034 interaction family, preferably after seeing whether the low-feature_024 and baseline feature_034 controls support a genuine joint concentration rather than a fragile selected subgroup effect.",
  "research_notes": "Accepted dataset-specific findings: H142, outcome_006 feature_060=1 vs 0 within feature_024 >= median; H146, high feature_024 quartile direct interaction, positive discovery +0.0583 and validation +0.0277, but imprecise and low confidence in magnitude. All outcome_006 claims direction -1; positive signed = stronger dependency. 10% threshold about 0.0175.\n\nCurrent priority: resolve the feature_024/feature_034 overlap. H152 remains the strongest nested simple effect but is unvalidated and selected. H153 is near null. H159/H160/H161 are active and directly test the median-high feature_034 interaction, high-third-quartile feature_034 simple effect, and high-third-quartile feature_034 interaction. New proposals add: low-feature_024 feature_034 interaction, low-feature_024 simple effect among feature_034=1, high-third-quartile feature_034=0 complement, baseline feature_034 effects in high and low feature_024, and outcome specificity for outcome_008/outcome_013 within high feature_024 and feature_034=1.\n\nInterpretation plan: if low-feature_024 feature_034 interaction is positive, feature_034 may be a main modifier and the accepted H142/H146 signal should not be framed as specifically feature_024-concentrated. If low-feature_024 interaction is null while high-feature_024 interaction is favorable, the evidence supports concentration in the feature_024-high and feature_034=1 intersection, but with careful multiple-threshold caveat. Baseline feature_034 effects should be checked before accepting H152-like intersection claims: a strong baseline feature_034 effect could explain part of the nested apparent interaction. If outcome_008/outcome_013 remain null in the intersection, outcome_006 specificity is strengthened.\n\nValidation budget: 5 remaining. Next validation target after analysis: H159, H161, or H152, depending on which contrast is both large and mechanistically central. Do not validate low-tail controls unless they unexpectedly become clinically large. Do not interpret accepted claims as causal or generalizable."
